---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
import { CodeBlock } from "@/components/ui/code-block";
---

<GameLayout title="OverTheWire: Semtex Level 8" gameName="semtex" level={8}>
    <h2 class="text-[18pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-2">
        Non-sniffable data
    </h2>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        This level is about some very simple covert channel, about transferring
        information that cannot possibly be sniffed. There is a socket file in
        /rdx/nature. It is a local Unix socket. Receive data from it until EOF
        and save it to a file.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Watch the time between the received bytes. Certain delays mean certain
        bytes that have been left out (have not been sent).
    </p>

    <CodeBlock client:visible
        >0-1 s : no special data 1-2 s : 'Q' 2-3 s : 'L' 3-4 s : 'A' 4-5 s : 'V'</CodeBlock
    >

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        you have to take these "unsent" data into your output file too, exactly
        at the places where they occur.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Thus you are receiving data while not receiving anything.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">The output file is a .jpg image :)</p>
</GameLayout>
